WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.879 --> 00:00:04.552
- After I got hurt, it was
painful to sit on the sidelines

00:00:04.552 --> 00:00:07.166
and watch other people play sports

00:00:07.166 --> 00:00:10.166
and participate and not be involved.

00:00:11.816 --> 00:00:14.245
When I started this
interest in photography,

00:00:14.245 --> 00:00:18.412
it was an opportunity to
get back into sports again.

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:24.125
My name is Loren Worthington
and I'm a photographer.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.304
When I was 21 years old, I
wanted to be a baseball player.

00:00:30.304 --> 00:00:34.295
I was playing one evening
and I hit a great double

00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:37.364
that was a lousy triple,
and I slid into third base,

00:00:37.364 --> 00:00:40.919
came in contact with
the other player's knee

00:00:40.919 --> 00:00:43.617
and it pinched my spinal cord.

00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:46.020
The result of that was paralysis.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.209
I'm a C5/6 quadriplegic.

00:00:48.209 --> 00:00:51.670
I've been in the wheelchair
for the past 30 years.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.446
It wasn't until almost
20 years after my injury

00:00:55.446 --> 00:00:57.613
that I picked up a camera.

00:01:00.229 --> 00:01:03.328
Adapting the camera is
kind of an extension

00:01:03.328 --> 00:01:05.809
of learning how to deal with a disability.

00:01:05.809 --> 00:01:09.082
I cannot use my right fingers.

00:01:09.082 --> 00:01:11.334
What I figured out is that I could use

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:14.458
an external shutter control with my mouth

00:01:14.458 --> 00:01:16.458
and take the photograph.

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:21.984
The type of photography
that I do is about people

00:01:21.984 --> 00:01:24.924
who are involved in
adaptive sports, and I felt

00:01:24.924 --> 00:01:28.198
my best photographs were of
people with disabilities

00:01:28.198 --> 00:01:32.365
because they saw in me somebody
that they could open up to.

00:01:33.666 --> 00:01:36.229
When I take photos of athletes,

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:40.518
I wanna show them as
somebody who works hard,

00:01:40.518 --> 00:01:43.039
who competes hard and who wants to win.

00:01:43.039 --> 00:01:47.206
It really shows more about the
athlete than the disability.

00:01:50.219 --> 00:01:52.860
When I first started
shooting adaptive sports,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.605
I immediately set my goal

00:01:54.605 --> 00:01:58.719
to taking photographs at the Paralympics.

00:01:58.719 --> 00:01:59.818
I got the phone call

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:02.082
from the United States Olympic Committee

00:02:02.082 --> 00:02:03.754
that they were interested in me

00:02:03.754 --> 00:02:06.421
going to Rio de Janeiro in 2016.

00:02:07.265 --> 00:02:09.887
There was some of the most
amazing athletes there

00:02:09.887 --> 00:02:11.481
and it worked out, same as what

00:02:11.481 --> 00:02:13.379
I've always had to deal with.

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:14.899
You just gotta try it.

00:02:14.899 --> 00:02:16.681
Probably the first day,
it's not gonna work so well

00:02:16.681 --> 00:02:19.032
but after that, you just start getting

00:02:19.032 --> 00:02:22.282
better and better at everything you do.

